1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,700
“I'll just move my stop
a little.” Here's what

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,500
that does.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,000
You planned to risk
fifty dollars. The trade

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,200
goes against you. You
move the stop. Now

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
you're risking a
hundred. Then a hundred

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:14,800
and fifty.

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,300
That's three times your
plan. And your journal

8
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,700
still says you had a
stop.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,200
Moving a stop further
away isn't managing the

10
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,400
trade. It's changing the
plan after the plan

11
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,200
stopped working.

12
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,500
If you do it, tag it.
Moved stop. Then check

13
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,100
what it cost you.

14
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,600
Be honest in the
comments. Have you ever

15
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,800
moved a stop?
